From: KOReader <https://github.com/koreader/koreader-base>
Subject: [PATCH] win32: build willuslib/win.c

`wsys.c` calls `win_has_own_window()` and `win_full_exe_name()` through its
`HAVE_WIN32_API` paths. MinGW enables those by defining `WIN32`, but the
functions live in `willuslib/win.c`, which the build does not include -- so the
link fails:

    undefined reference to `win_has_own_window'
    undefined reference to `win_full_exe_name'

(Replaces `win32_drop_wgui.patch` and `win32_no_ansi_parse.patch`, which were
written against the previous libk2pdfopt pin, `1fcffeb`. Upstream's update to
`64aa9cc` (ffac0764, #2542) dropped `wgui.c` from the build and made
`avprintf()` call `vfprintf()` unconditionally, so both of those changes are now
upstream's; only this one is still needed.)

--- a/lib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,11 @@ add_library(k2pdfopt
     ../willuslib/wleptonica.c
     ../willuslib/wsys.c
 )
+if(WIN32)
+    # NOTE: `wsys.c` calls into these through its `HAVE_WIN32_API` paths,
+    #       which only get enabled on Windows (see `willuslib/willus.h`).
+    target_sources(k2pdfopt PRIVATE ../willuslib/win.c)
+endif()
 set_target_properties(k2pdfopt PROPERTIES SOVERSION 2)
 set_target_properties(k2pdfopt PROPERTIES
     C_VISIBILITY_PRESET hidden
